{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity","id":1482108,"title":"Immunity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-27T15:35:56-07:00","id":1482108,"title":"Immunity","content":"So, I was rereading a Mage book yesterday and I stumbled upon que Merit &quot;Immunity&quot; and I was impressed I didn't remember it well, because it's the most broken Merit I've ever seen. With enough points, the character can be completely immune to physical attacks and even damage from any source altogether (besides something absurdly rare if you put a lot of points into it). I mean, it can certainly be cool for an NPC, an antagonist, etc, but it's hard to imagine one ST allowing pcs to have it. <br /> So, my question is have you ever used this Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T19:12:05-07:00","id":1482117,"title":"","content":"No, I haven't. But I think it could be cool at it's &quot;lower&quot; levels to represent some exotic character type. Like, a certain element immunity as part of being an elemental-related Nephilim.<br /> <br /> In general, I think of it as a very exotic thing. I don't like it a whole lot for pc. I think that at high levels of expenditure it has the same potential of being &quot;broken&quot; as it has of being a trap, depending on how important it's going to be surviving a &quot;conventional&quot; combat.<br /> <br /> Tougths:<br /> <br /> *You're the <i>potential </i>perfect &quot;tank&quot; - but tanks are supposed to be &quot;unstoppable&quot;, not just &quot;unbreakable&quot;. Since you've put your everything into that Merit, you're not likely to be able to do much else on the short notice. Even the densest of Werewolves would eventually get the memo that &quot;clawing you even harder&quot; it's not going to work, and just grab you and put you under a rock or something :P<br /> There's a millon ways to deal with enemies that don't involve hitting them with damage dice, and some are concerningly common. For some vampires &quot;Dominate the mortal&quot; it's more of a ready-to-go first tactic than Potence. In Mage I would argue you're often more at risk of being captured and sent to Room 101 (yes, as a Technocrat too) than just killed. In a Traditions game, &quot;rescue character from Technocratic facility&quot; it's as cliched as for Vampire it's &quot;getting a mission from the Prince&quot;.<br /> <br /> *It's, maybe, a munchkin's wet dream, since it trivializes such a basic aspect of combat, but it can easily become a nedless burden if the chronicle isn't too geared towards situations that would cause &quot;damage&quot;. Since it's nearly useless outside such conventional figths, and it also <i>trivializes </i>them, I think it has the potential to be quite <b><i>boring</i></b>. Which may be the harshest judgement that I can have about something on a game. Altrough, as said, haven't tested it so I can't be sure.<br /> <br /> *Immortal 7pts of BoS, while less &quot;absolute&quot;, may be a more fun option for those PC with a serious survival issue (like say, a mage that wants to &quot;run with werewolves&quot;). Simply put, you will survive after dying by normal means BUT you're still better off if you don't suffer trough that, thus given incentives to &quot;not dying&quot;. Plus, you don't need to &quot;exhaust&quot; your character sheet on it.<br /> <br /> *As said, for an antagonist it's interesting because it could be fun for the players to think and research about solutions to the problem with the versatility of magick.<br /> <br /> *I think Paradox can become whatever it's your weakness for purposes of damage. A lot of it's forms aren't about damage anyway. Hobgoblins and spirits could actually <i>reveal</i> your weakness for the world to see","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-27-2022, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T20:45:47-07:00","id":1482124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As said, for an antagonist it's interesting because it could be fun for the players to think and research about solutions to the problem with the versatility of magick. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, basically it's the only thing I could think of as interesting from a narrative point of view. Especially when you deal with powergamers as a ST, it's sometimes interesting to come up with an antagonist who just can't be beaten in &quot;normal combat&quot;, no matter how absolutely broken your pc character is. It has the potential to force unredeemable power gamers to &quot;think outside the box&quot; when they see that no matter the fact that they cause zillion damage per turn, it doesn't mean shit and the said antagonist could then be beaten by something as simple as salt lol...<br /> <br /> I asked more because of this, in the perspective to change the overall perception of &quot;how to defeat an enemy&quot; and my curiosity is also concerned to know if anyone has ever used it in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T07:22:12-07:00","id":1482154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482124#post1482124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, basically it's the only thing I could think of as interesting from a narrative point of view. Especially when you deal with powergamers as a ST, it's sometimes interesting to come up with an antagonist who just can't be beaten in &quot;normal combat&quot;, no matter how absolutely broken your pc character is. It has the potential to force unredeemable power gamers to &quot;think outside the box&quot; when they see that no matter the fact that they cause zillion damage per turn, it doesn't mean shit and the said antagonist could then be beaten by something as simple as salt lol...<br /> <br /> I asked more because of this, in the perspective to change the overall perception of &quot;how to defeat an enemy&quot; and my curiosity is also concerned to know if anyone has ever used it in their games.</div> </div> </div> </div>In D&amp;D, I had a Greater Barghest as an antagonist in a low level adventure, where his goal involved leaving the party alive. It was a group of four 3rd level characters. He stayed in the woods and organized hunting to ensure his goblin worshipers could eat and multiply. In the multi-tribe alliance, he had established a tradition where goblins approaching old age would organize into attack units and besiege farmers on the edge of town. They would kill livestock with crossbows to provoke the farmers, for who they saved their <i>special</i> arrows. These weren't meant to kill, but create a painful debilitating injury.<br /> <br /> The involuntary screams of those struck provided sound cover. The veteran units, who had started their siege at night, would move silently and reposition themselves. Since they had no plans to survive, they would remain awake for up to forty eight hours, terrorizing the town.<br /> <br /> The town faced a difficult choice; call for the Duke's army to establish a fort there, charging heavy taxes for the expense, or put out a call for adventurers with generous store prices as a reward. The later choice brought the 1st level adventurers to this troubled frontier. The party levelled and made a fortune taking down packs of humanoids, among other adventures, leading up to the encounter with the Barghest at 3rd level. <br /> <br /> He wore them down until it was obvious they would die if the fight continued, whereupon he offered a truce. The party agreed never to attack the members of his tribe again and were allowed to keep all their gear. He took his leave, walked out of view, turned invisible and snuck back into their midst... to <i>listen</i> (that version had Detect Thoughts).<br /> <br /> In a sorry state, the party regrouped to discuss how they were going to get back to town, which other adventures they should pursue that did not violate the truce and, most important to the Invisible Barghest, <i>who</i> they would go to for aid. The discussion revealed most of the important NPCs the players and the town relied on - the healer-priest at the temple, the mage, guard captain, etcetera.<br /> <br /> A few weeks later, the Barghest and his most elite agents carried out a series of assassinations. They took out all of the important spellcasters, official message cryptographer, the stablemaster, killed all of the horses the could and left caltrops all over the main road to discourage travel on foot. They effectively severed communication between the town and the rest of civilization. <br /> <br /> The party had been deliberately left with riches and a lot of inside knowledge about the inner workings of the town, for who they were now the only group with spellcasting and other in-demand skills. The Barghest, using disguise and charms, spread rumors that the party had aided him in his assassination spree, in return for their lives and for the opportunity to be installed in power to serve his evil ends. This split the town between those who believed in the heroes and those who gave into the hysteria.<br /> <br /> The next two sessions - about four hours each - were almost entirely dialogue, with dice being rolled only to determine outcomes of social skill checks. It was more intense than combat and made for some deep character development. All this was possible, because I used a monster who, relative to the PCs in challenge rating, was invincible...<br /> <br /> Currently, in Mage, I have a Technomancer with Time 4, using both Contingency and Time-Stop to facilitate his nefarious plans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T19:27:05-07:00","id":1482320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482117#post1482117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*It's, maybe, a munchkin's wet dream, since it trivializes such a basic aspect of combat, but it can easily become a nedless burden if the chronicle isn't too geared towards situations that would cause &quot;damage&quot;. Since it's nearly useless outside such conventional figths, and it also <i>trivializes </i>them, I think it has the potential to be quite <b><i>boring</i></b>. Which may be the harshest judgement that I can have about something on a game. Altrough, as said, haven't tested it so I can't be sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in Mage, actually, but I've seen one or two such characters.<br /> <br /> Being boring on the hands of PCs depends a lot on the players and ST.<br /> <br /> As said, immunity itself isn't as worth as it sounds at first. It forces some thinking outside the box, but once that's done it is quite trivial to deal with. Even an All-in-Potence Vampire can just grab you and throw away.<br /> <br /> Yet, it opens an avenue for the more proactive players. More important than how the Immune character operates in a fight, this character can deal with problems in unconventional ways since they don't need to take the same precautions as everyone else. buoy on lava, enter high voltage generators with it on, you can specialize in identifying cars by the feel of being overrun by them. Exploring those new avenues is a lot of fun, and increases your options without really making things too easy or boring, just new.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-29T21:12:20-07:00","id":1482338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Being boring on the hands of PCs depends a lot on the players and ST. </div> </div> </div>Exactly my thought here, for once I'm considering using an antagonist with this merit as it creates a &quot;change of pace&quot; for players who are more than used to the idea of overwhelming everything through sheer force. &quot;Potential to be boring&quot;, anything has really, because, as everything else in the game, it will always depend on the PCs and the ST. And talking about &quot;boring&quot;, I think that simply giving the big baddie a larger soak dice pool is usually much more &quot;boring&quot; than making the group try to find the enemy weakness, once they find out they &quot;can't beat&quot; him using &quot;conventional means&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T08:41:31-07:00","id":1482374,"title":"","content":"As monteparnas says with the right players it can actually open alot of doors. It depends on how you leverage it. The outright invulnerability is interesting if used in a limited way (the 'lower' levels of the merit) but the higher cost ones get boring (and IMHO if you use it for powergaming, you're just gonna invite creative punishments from the Storyteller, which I think motivates the player to collaborate actively in working out the parameters.) As the merit itself noted it doesn't necessarily protect against secondary effects or ancillary effects (destruction of stuff you wear or carry, for example... but this can extend to pain, blood loss, etc. depending on how it works. Pain will still carry the dice penalties, and blood loss would still need to be stabilized even if it won't kill you. Worse, all that blood is evidence left behind at a potential scene that could be used to locate you... or might be used by some supernatural being in some ritualistic manner.) Or there may be indirect ways to trigger it (immunity to bullets or physical injury might work if it touches your body, but not if it transmits blunt trauma through stuff you're wearing, like the in-book example.) <br /> <br /> In the end it's clear the way the merit is applied is very open ended, as well as in how you balance the cost/benefit dynamic and that is very much up to the players and storyteller to work out, and in that respect it's not different than other similar merits (like 'Immortal' - which is a close analogue to immunity and plays on alot of the Highlander stereotypes again, as does immunity itself.) <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25533,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","user":"Mister_Dunpeal","date":". 05-30-2022, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T09:43:16-07:00","id":1482379,"title":"","content":"On the player side, my friend is playing his dream girl, a character he brought to life through art for years before deciding to play her in Mage. She has Correspondence and Time both at 3. In session zero, for the purpose of familiarizing newbies with the magic system, I gave an example of a rote such a dimensionalist could use to stay safe. <i>&quot;</i>Tracers<i>&quot;</i> allows the caster to jog or run while not being at any specific point they are moving through. Bullets miss. <br /> <br /> She has high Dexterity and Athletics, which she uses to cast this rote. Her mid range Arcane rating avoids sleepers paying too much attention the effect. To avoid it being overpowered, I stipulated that it requires concentration for as long as it is in use. It's reminiscent of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uz2-D4lY2qg\" target=\"_blank\">Run Lola Run</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T12:40:45-07:00","id":1482394,"title":"","content":"Honest Opinion? The merit isn't as good as people think it is and is Way overpriced.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really protect against anything important to the game. Your mage might be immune to damage, but does that really help them That much? It doesn't make ascending any easier, it doesn't give them any powers that could overthrow/preserve the technocracy, doesn't protect their friends family or stuff, doesn't prevent them from getting captured/tortured/brainwashed/trapped/tricked/etc.<br /> <br /> The Only thing it's useful for is combat, but the WoD is rarely a combat heavy game(outside WtA). A character that takes it is going to quickly realize that they're in a highlander-type situation where they'll watch their friends, family, home, possessions, country, beliefs, and ideology all die as they persist ever onward...<br /> <br /> I'd take Medium and Spark of Life over it it any day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-30-2022, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-30T14:57:45-07:00","id":1482410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482394#post1482394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The merit isn't as good as people think it is and is Way overpriced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. I, too, think it's vastly overpriced. That's why I say it could be a trap or a burden. To get a strong Immunity you have to expend ALL your freebies, basically, and then maybe buy Defects and spend those points on it, too. So it <i>better </i>come into play a lot...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:14:47-07:00","id":1482510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn't really protect against anything important to the game. Your mage might be immune to damage, but does that really help them That much? </div> </div> </div>This one made me laugh lol<br /> <br /> After this one I give up having any meaningful discussion about the merit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T11:42:08-07:00","id":1482517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482510#post1482510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This one made me laugh lol<br /> <br /> After this one I give up having any meaningful discussion about the merit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can't tell if you're being sarcastic here...<br /> <br /> I agree with Aleph and Prometheas, it's not a great Merit. It's very expensive, and just being able to survive any damage isn't really as useful as it at first sounds. You'll have low willpower and Arete since you didn't have any available freebies to spend. An enemy can just mind control you, or bury you alive for a few hundred years just to see how insane you become, and if you're buried without access to materials, you aren't gaining xp and so you likely can't even escape if you can't increase your Arete or Spheres<br /> <br /> It doesn't sound like a fun character to me.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would disallow it. As a player, I would definitely not want to buy it.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:12:18-07:00","id":1482523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>breggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482517#post1482517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't tell if you're being sarcastic here...<br /> <br /> I agree with Aleph and Prometheas, it's not a great Merit. It's very expensive, and just being able to survive any damage isn't really as useful as it at first sounds. You'll have low willpower and Arete since you didn't have any available freebies to spend. An enemy can just mind control you, or bury you alive for a few hundred years just to see how insane you become, and if you're buried without access to materials, you aren't gaining xp and so you likely can't even escape if you can't increase your Arete or Spheres<br /> <br /> It doesn't sound like a fun character to me.<br /> <br /> As an ST, I would disallow it. As a player, I would definitely not want to buy it.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it's pretty obvious that I'm being sarcastic. If someone tells me it's IRRELEVANT to be IMMUNE TO DAMAGE, then I have nothing to argue with this person anymore, for the sake of my own sanity lol. I'm not going to say more because it would probably be against the forum rules lol. The thing is even funny...<br /> <br /> Of course a ST can troll any PC with ANY POWER. One could be Porthos or Voormas and still be fucked up, but that doesn't change a fact. To state that being immune to damage is &quot;inconsequential&quot; is utterly beyond any adjective I could use here without breaking the forum rules, so I won't argue about it.<br /> <br /> As a player (not that I'm ever a player, as since my childhood I basically only ST) I would probably never buy it, and I'd surely disallow it as a ST, but that doesn't change the fact that it's broken beyond measure.<br /> <br /> Even sophism must have its limits...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 05-31-2022, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:32:13-07:00","id":1482528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482523#post1482523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think it's pretty obvious that I'm being sarcastic. If someone tells me it's IRRELEVANT to be IMMUNE TO DAMAGE, then I have nothing to argue with this person anymore, for the sake of my own sanity lol. I'm not going to say more because it would probably be against the forum rules lol. The thing is even funny...<br /> <br /> Of course a ST can troll any PC with ANY POWER. One could be Porthos or Voormas and still be fucked up, but that doesn't change a fact. To state that being immune to damage is &quot;inconsequential&quot; is utterly beyond any adjective I could use here without breaking the forum rules, so I won't argue about it.<br /> <br /> As a player (not that I'm ever a player, as since my childhood I basically only ST) I would probably never buy it, and I'd surely disallow it as a ST, but that doesn't change the fact that it's broken beyond measure.<br /> <br /> Even sophism must have its limits...</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really think anyone was saying it's *irrelevant*... or at least saying that is more hyperbole than literal.<br /> <br /> It's broken, sure, but only in one very specific way, and taking that merit would weaken and break a character in just about every other way. An enemy might punch them... huh, that was weird. So they pull out a laser rifle and.... wow, that was really weird. Ok, I can't kill this guy, so I'll just hold him down until I can figure out what to do with him. It's not like he can do anything to stop me from holding him down with his rank 1 spheres and low attributes and abilities.<br /> <br /> I learned years ago that trying to powergame by making a &quot;one trick pony&quot; type character is not a fun way to roleplay. It just doesn't work out in practice the way you had hoped it would when you came up with the idea.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26904-breggie","name":"breggie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26904_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T12:57:19-07:00","id":1482532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, I can't kill this guy, so I'll just hold him down until I can figure out what to do with him </div> </div> </div>You're just forgetting the guy has actions and he's A MAGE, so after the punch he just &quot;booms&quot; (even before the laser lol), so the merit alone would skyrocket the level of threat's perception the mage offers, besides many people wanting to understand him or bring him to their cause, discounting the fact that he could one day become a master. Now Imagine Porthos immune to physical damage and then we can talk about what this merit means. The fact that it exists is good as it can create different kind of stories that could be interesting, but it alone makes the character more resilient than any Methuselah level vampire per the official rules (although, to be fair, given the crappy defensive powers the developers of vampires have created throughout the years, it's not a big deal lol). Now imagine Porthos, but more resilient than Karsh (or any werewolf for the matter lol), then we have a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T13:01:52-07:00","id":1482533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I learned years ago that trying to powergame by making a &quot;one trick pony&quot; type character is not a fun way to roleplay. It just doesn't work out in practice the way you had hoped it would when you came up with the idea. </div> </div> </div>In no point I said anyone was trying to &quot;powergame&quot; with it. I just mentioned the merit and wanted to discuss its possibilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> or at least saying that is more hyperbole than literal. </div> </div> </div>That's what I meant all along...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T14:48:42-07:00","id":1482542,"title":"","content":"If a merit costs fifteen freebie points, I want it to manifest outside the game as this invincible character, leave my apartment and ask the guy across the hall to turn down Cannibal Corpse... politely. Even said benefit would be a questionable tradeoff for having to start with Arete 1, unless I only played the character once. <br /> <br /> Supposing there was a seven point version that acted like the Stone Skin spell from D&amp;D, I could picture two interesting builds. Both would have:<br /> <br /> 7 points allocated to Mental Attributes so I could take specialties in Intel and Perception,<br /> Arete 3, <br /> <br /> The first character would have Prime 3, Spirit 3. Basically, &quot;Technocracy, I'm going to bust your gauntlet as often as I please, because I have places to be. And Paradox, I'll deal with you later.&quot; <br /> <br /> The second would have Mind 3, Time 1, Correspondence 1 and Entropy 1, with ambitions to raise the last three all to 2. The role of this character would be to ascertain threats to the Cabal, keep people apprised via Mind-link and tank for whoever needed it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-31T17:02:38-07:00","id":1482553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1482108-immunity?p=1482523#post1482523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a player (not that I'm ever a player, as since my childhood I basically only ST) I would probably never buy it, and I'd surely disallow it as a ST, but that doesn't change the fact that it's broken beyond measure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is irrelevant at all. But I do think it is overpriced and not broken by any measure. At least, not in Mage.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. In Mage the ultimate factor to define if something is strong is to define how hard it is to emulate, surpass or bypass it using Magic (anything that directly affects your casting is automatically stronger than anything else). The secondary factors are how likely it is to A) help you accomplish your goals against other Mages and B) hinder other Mages in messing with your plans.<br /> <br /> So, what Immunity actually brings to the table?<br /> <br /> Protecting yourself against damage is one of the first things most Mages worry about and can be accomplished with any Sphere. Magical protections against specific sources of damage can be incredibly effective. So all in all emulating it isn't that hard and begins at virtually any Sphere at levels 2 or 3.<br /> <br /> You can also make magic that not only protects you from damage, but also uses the source to trigger other effects, heal you, or whatever, so surpassing it is also doable, depends more on Sphere, but nothing too problematic and solidly on level 3.<br /> <br /> Bypass it is equally simple. Magic to hold, to transport, to transform, to suffocate, dehydrate and starve. Of course is isn't standard, but once causing damage proves a problem it isn't hard for any Mage to find other ways to eliminate you from the equation.<br /> <br /> What goals does it help you to accomplish? Not dying is certainly a nice one, but not the hardest most of the time. As I said before, being able to ignore damage does give you options for so many task, but those options will rarely be incredibly more effective, just innovative. It will only help you scenarios where achieving your goal involves risking damage, which in Mage isn't as common as it seems at first, because the characters always have too many resources to avoid damage in the first place.<br /> <br /> Finally, how does it hinders other Mages? Not much, actually, because the only thing it hinders at all is the eventual goal of causing you damage or killing you, which again won't be as frequent as it seems. Violence is usually a means to an end, and Mages have too many resources to achieve their ends avoiding violence, and even when it involves violence they don't need to kill the other party. They may try to rob you, kidnap you, possess you, dismantle your influence, take over your house, control your assets, and nothing here necessarily demands your death.<br /> <br /> Certainly a strong benefit. Hardly game breaking. Definitely not worth its cost. I allow it no problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}